---
description: Provider layout, SDK pin and generated docs. Read before editing internal/provider, docs or templates.
globs: internal/provider/**,docs/**,templates/**,examples/**,GNUmakefile
alwaysApply: false
---

- Everything lives in `internal/provider/`. `provider.go` and `client.go` hold configuration and authentication: treat them as high risk and leave them alone unless the ticket names them.
- One file per resource, data source, action or ephemeral resource, with its `_test.go` beside it. Unit tests use `httptest`; they need no secrets and no server.
- The API client is the generated Go SDK pinned in `go.mod`. Do not bump, replace or regenerate it unless the ticket says so. If the SDK is wrong, use a request editor or a local decode struct in the file you are changing.
- `docs/` is generated by `make docs` from schema descriptions, `templates/` and `examples/`. Never hand-edit generated docs. Commit only the doc files your change affects.
- The repository is public: no private links, internal ticket IDs, credentials, customer names or local paths in code, comments, fixtures or docs. Fixtures use `example.com` data.
